  "keyTakeaways": [
    "U.S. Chapter 32 exports fell 4.1% to $7.78B in 2025; paints and varnishes (3208–3210, $2.80B) held almost flat, while titanium dioxide pigment (3206.11) dropped 18.4% to $873M.",
    "Canada and Mexico buy 51% and charge nothing on goods that qualify for USMCA, and the EU, the third-largest market at $898M, has charged nothing on any U.S. Chapter 32 good since July 1, 2026.",
    "China is the only large buyer that raised tariffs — a 10% extra duty on top of 2019 counter-tariffs — and exports there fell 21.6% to $289M; watch December 31, 2026 (its exclusions end) and January 10, 2027 (its 24-point suspension ends).",
    "January–August 2026 exports were up 1.2% on the same months of 2025, led by Canada (+3.9%) and strong gains in Brazil (+31.8%) and India (+32.8%)."
  ],
